#
# TSan suppressions for oneTBB's partitioners, used by the tbb_validation tests
# of a SANITIZER=thread build (examples/validation/CMakeLists.txt).
#
# A parallel_for task is built by one worker -- the root by the caller, each
# split-off child by the worker that splits (start_for's constructors: its
# range, its partitioner state, its copy of the body) -- and run by another
# that steals it. The spawn and the steal synchronise inside libtbb.so, which
# is not instrumented: TSan misses that happens-before edge and reports every
# field of the new task (blocked_range::is_divisible, check_being_stolen's
# my_divisor, the body's members) as a race with its constructor.
#
# A suppression matches when ANY frame of a reported stack matches: this one
# matches the write side of those reports, the task's construction. The code
# under test runs in execute() -> run_body(), not under a constructor of
# start_for (except the body's copy constructor): its races stay visible.
race:tbb::detail::d1::start_for*::start_for

# The wait tree (partitioner.h): the caller's wait_node and each split's
# tree_node are built by one thread and folded (fold_tree) by the last child
# to finish, on another; the root's wait_node sits on the caller's stack, at
# the same address from one parallel_for to the next. Ordered inside
# libtbb.so (the wait_context, the reference counts' release), unseen. No
# body runs there: shrink_array::tbb has no reduction, whose join() fold_tree
# would call.
race:tbb::detail::d1::node::node
race:tbb::detail::d1::fold_tree

# The execution_data of a running task (detail/_task.h), filled in by
# libtbb.so (the arena's slots, set up in task_arena::initialize) and read
# inline by the task: no body runs in these readers. (is_stolen also covers
# partitioner.h's is_stolen_task.)
race:tbb::detail::d1::original_slot
race:tbb::detail::d1::affinity_slot
race:tbb::detail::d1::execution_slot
race:tbb::detail::d1::is_same_affinity
race:tbb::detail::d1::is_stolen

# A finished task (start_for::finalize: read my_parent, destroy the task, fold
# the tree, hand the memory back) and the next task built at the same address:
# the small_object_allocator's recycling happens inside libtbb.so, unseen. Not
# start_for::run, which the caller thread runs the body under.
race:tbb::detail::d1::start_for*::finalize
